  "decision": "HOLD",
  "fix_description": "Finding 1 (high, line 6): sanitize repo_url before use. Reject or allow-list URLs, enforce an http(s):// or git@ scheme prefix, and reject any value starting with '-'. When invoking git clone, insert '--' before repo_url so it is not treated as a git option: subprocess.run(['git','clone','--depth','1','--',repo_url,dest], ...). Also verify repo_url matches an approved prefix and does not contain shell metacharacters. Finding 2 (low, line 14): the pytest command is fixed and shell=False, so no direct command injection is present; harden it by asserting workdir is an existing absolute path, avoiding untrusted cwd, and keeping CI_TOKEN removed from the environment before invoking subprocess. Both fixes are safe and idempotent.",
